{
  "name": "Fill missing WordPress image alt text with OpenAI and Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3c80fcc3-875a-4e67-95cd-51f33df1ec6d",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1100,
        "content": "## Auto-fill missing WordPress image alt text with context-aware AI (no plugins)\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow finds WordPress media items that are missing image alt text, skips items already logged, enriches each image with the title and excerpt of the post or page it is attached to, and uses a vision-capable LLM to generate context-aware alt text in your chosen language. In **review mode (default)** suggestions are logged to Google Sheets as `pending`; change a row's `status` to `approved` (edit the text first if you like) and the hourly run writes it to WordPress. In **auto mode** alt text is written to WordPress immediately and logged.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- **WordPress:** Users \u2192 Profile \u2192 *Application Passwords* \u2192 create one. Add a WordPress API credential (site URL, username, application password) and select it in every WordPress HTTP Request node.\n- **Google Sheets:** create one tab named `Log` with this header row:\n`media_id | image_url | admin_url | post_title | alt_text | is_decorative | confidence | status | updated_at`\nConnect your Google Sheets credential in all four Sheets nodes.\n- **AI model:** add OpenAI credentials, or swap the chat model for Claude, Gemini or any other vision-capable model.\n- **Config:** fill in `wp_base_url` (no trailing slash), `sheet_id`, `alt_language`, `mode` and `max_per_run`.\n- Test with `max_per_run = 5` via **Manual Trigger** and check the sheet before activating the schedules.\n\n### Important \u2014 scope\n\nThis updates the alt text stored on the **media library item**. WordPress stores alt text for images already placed inside post content in the post HTML, so those existing in-content images are **not** changed. Featured images, galleries, WooCommerce product images and future inserts use the new alt text.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange `max_per_run` to control batch size and AI cost, `max_alt_length` for alt text length, or the prompt rules inside the LLM chain for your preferred style."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0bb3ab00-0a71-41b3-968e-06c26e55aa0e",
